t":"2013-10-20T10:10:11Z","body":"By the way the message content is not properly formatted: it should be line splitted and each line should be prefixed by `data:`.\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/playframework/playframework/issues/comments/26670165/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"julienrf","id":332812,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMjgxMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/332812?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/julienrf","html_url":"https://github.com/julienrf","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/julienrf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/julienrf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/julienrf/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/julienrf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/julienrf/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/julienrf/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/julienrf/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/julienrf/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/julienrf/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/playframework/playframework/issues/comments/26686906","html_url":"https://github.com/playframework/playframework/issues/1862#issuecomment-26686906","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/playframework/playframework/issues/1862","id":26686906,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI2Njg2OTA2","user":{"login":"jroper","id":105833,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNTgzMw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105833?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jroper","html_url":"https://github.com/jroper","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jroper/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jroper/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jroper/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jroper/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jroper/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jroper/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jroper/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jroper/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jroper/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2013-10-21T00:22:13Z","updated_at":"2013-10-21T00:22:13Z","body":"Actually the Scala library has this exact issue too, when publishing Strings, it uses the comet String encoder, see here:\n\nhttps://github.com/playframework/playframework/blob/master/framework/src/play/src/main/scala/play/api/libs/Comet.scala\n\nThat's why I did the escaping.  The difference between the Scala and the Java libraries is that Scala supports publishing JSON directly, which is what everyone always uses, so you never notice it.\n\nSo, to solve this, we can, like the Java comet support, overload sendData to accept JsonNode.\n\nAnd then we should fix both the Scala and the Java string encoding support.  The reason why it does that now, I think, is to ensure that the content is on one line.  What needs to happen, I think, is if there are multiple lines, each line needs to be prepended with `data`.\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/playframework/playframework/issues/comments/26686906/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"jroper","id":105833,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNTgzMw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105833?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jroper","html_url":"https://github.com/jroper","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jroper/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jroper/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jroper/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jroper/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jroper/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jroper/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jroper/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jroper/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jroper/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/playframework/playframework/issues/comments/27695145","html_url":"https://github.com/playframework/playframework/issues/1862#issuecomment-27695145","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/playframework/playframework/issues/1862","id":27695145,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI3Njk1MTQ1","user":{"login":"julienrf","id":332812,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMjgxMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/332812?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/julienrf","html_url":"https://github.com/julienrf","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/julienrf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/julienrf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/julienrf/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/julienrf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/julienrf/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/julienrf/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/julienrf/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/julienrf/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/julienrf/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2013-11-04T15:47:46Z","updated_at":"2013-11-04T15:47:46Z","body":"> And then we should fix both the Scala and the Java string encoding support. The reason why it does that now, I think, is to ensure that the content is on one line. What needs to happen, I think, is if there are multiple lines, each line needs to be prepended with data.\n\nHow to fix that without breaking backward compatibility? (the Scala API would be even harder to fix without breaking things)\n\nIn summary we want to support sending JSON values as well as String values. We’d also want to have a good support of name and id attributes that are specific to the EventSource protocol. The current way to deal with these attributes is to provide variants of the `sendData` method with additional parameters, but this approach would be cumbersome to follow: if we wanted to add an overload to support JSON data instead of String data, we would have to actually add three overloads instead of just one.\n\nNote that if the current way of sending String values did not escape their content, sending JSON as Stringified values would just work (no need to overload `sendData`).\n\nWe could fix the Java API by deprecating the current `sendData*` methods and adding a method with the following signature:\n\n``` java\nvoid send(Data data)\n```\n\nWhere `Data` is a static inner class of `EventSource` having a builder-like API to make EventSource messages. E.g.:\n\n``` java\neventSource.send(new Data(\"foo\"));\n\neventSource.send(new Data(\"foo\").withName(\"name\").withId(\"42\"));\n\neventSource.send(new Data(Json.stringify(jsonValue)));\n```\n\nWDYT?\n\nI can not find a nice way to fix the Scala API without breaking backward compatibility, though. I would just replace the `CometMessage[E]` type usage with another type that would be specific to EventSource and would do the serialization in the right way.\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/playframework/playframework/issues/comments/27695145/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"julienrf","id":332812,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMjgxMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/332812?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/julienrf","html_url":"https://github.com/julienrf","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/julienrf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/julienrf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/julienrf/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/julienrf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/julienrf/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/julienrf/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/julienrf/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/julienrf/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/julienrf/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/playframework/playframework/issues/comments/27731672","html_url":"https://github.com/playframework/playframework/issues/1862#issuecomment-27731672","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/playframework/playframework/issues/1862","id":27731672,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI3NzMxNjcy","user":{"login":"jroper","id":105833,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNTgzMw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105833?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jroper","html_url":"https://github.com/jroper","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jroper/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jroper/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jroper/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jroper/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jroper/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jroper/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jroper/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jroper/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jroper/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2013-11-04T22:58:09Z","updated_at":"2013-11-04T22:58:09Z","body":"I'm not too concerned about breaking backwards compatibility in the Scala API here - what we have now is broken, and besides, who uses event source with anything but JSON?  I suspect no one, otherwise this issue would have been raised a lot sooner, as it happens it was only noticed after the same problem was noticed in the Java API.\n\nI think the Data class is a good idea.  Except, I would call it Event, and have a static factory method event() so that it can be created nicely.\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/playframework/playframework/issues/comments/27731672/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"jroper","id":105833,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNTgzMw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105833?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jroper","html_url":"https://github.com/jroper","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jroper/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jroper/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jroper/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jroper/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jroper/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jroper/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jroper/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jroper/